# eviimission.com forwards to the offering on Issuance Express.
# Ben Young, Issuance Express, Aug 6 2026: the deal page cannot be displayed
# on our domain, it must be an actual forwarding, because the investor has to
# look up at their browser and see that they are on Issuance Express.
#
# index.html and images/ stay in the repo. That file is still what we hand to
# Issuance. The forced catch-all below shadows it rather than deleting it.
#
# The legacy paths are redundant while the catch-all exists, but if the
# catch-all is ever removed to restore the page, these still resolve.

# Images are exempt, and this rule must stay above the catch-all, because the
# engine takes the first matching rule reading top to bottom.
#
# og:image, og:image:secure_url, twitter:image, three JSON-LD contentUrls and a
# VideoObject thumbnailUrl are all absolute to this domain. Without this rule
# the catch-all's ! shadows the real files, so every one of those URLs answers
# with an HTML redirect instead of an image and every share preview renders
# blank: LinkedIn, X, iMessage, WhatsApp, Slack, Facebook.
#
# Ben's rule is that the deal PAGE cannot be displayed here. A JPEG is not the
# deal page. Assets stay on a domain we control so the card cannot break if
# Issuance reorganises their paths.
/images/*   /images/:splat   200

/evi        https://issuanceexpress.com/evii-mission  301!
/evi/*      https://issuanceexpress.com/evii-mission  301!
/invest     https://issuanceexpress.com/evii-mission  301!
/invest/*   https://issuanceexpress.com/evii-mission  301!
/round3     https://issuanceexpress.com/evii-mission  301!
/highlander https://issuanceexpress.com/evii-mission  301!

# Everything else, including /. The ! forces it ahead of any real file.
/*          https://issuanceexpress.com/evii-mission  301!
